course: dictionary
lesson: 3660
title: A person who catches fish
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: A fisherman is a person who catches fish, either as a job or just for fun. More than one is fishermen. When you meet a word you do not know, look at the words around it for clues.
explain: «Hamish's dad is a fisherman in Inverness» tells you that fisherman names a job someone can do. Swap in your meaning: "Hamish's dad is a person who catches fish in Inverness." It still makes sense, so your meaning is right.
explain: «A fishing boat» and «a keen fisherman» give more clues. A fishing boat is a boat used to catch fish, and a keen fisherman is someone who loves fishing and does it often. Stories can use the word too, such as «the old fisherman» in a folk tale.
fact: A fisherman is a person who catches fish, as a job or for fun.
fact: The plural of fisherman is fishermen.
fact: «A fishing boat» is a boat used to catch fish.
fact: «A keen fisherman» is someone who loves fishing and does it often.
exercise: «Hamish's dad is a fisherman in Inverness.» What is a fisherman? | Someone who sells fish in a shop only | A person who cooks fish in a restaurant | A boat that carries people across a river | *A person who catches fish, as a job or for fun
exercise: Which word is the plural of fisherman? | *fishermen | fishers | fishermens | fishingmen
exercise: What is a fishing boat? | *A boat used to catch fish | A boat for carrying cars across the water | A boat with no engine and no sails | A boat that is used only in harbours for parties
test: Swap the meaning into «Jesus called fishermen such as Peter, Andrew, James and John.» Which meaning still makes sense? | A person who builds houses | A person who reads books | A person who lives on the moon | *A person who catches fish
test: What does «a keen fisherman» mean? | Someone who sells cars | *Someone who loves fishing and does it often | Someone who is angry all the time | Someone who never leaves home
exam: What is the plural of fisherman? | fishers | fishingmen | fishermens | *fishermen
